== 1. Claude Code fixes the bug (no chloe MCP, no memory_save) ==
The tests failed because `page_count` used floor division (`//`), which rounds down and drops a partial last page, so 21 items gave 2 pages and 3 items gave 0. I changed it to ceiling division, `-(-total_items // per_page)`, and all 3 tests now pass.

Skipped: `per_page <= 0` still raises or misbehaves, and I didn't add a guard. No tests cover that case or `total_items == 0` (which returns 0 pages).
